devkit does not bundle third-party code. At install time it downloads, from their upstream repositories at the
pinned commits listed in config/skills.json, the following agent skills, which remain under their own licences:

  mattpocock/skills                 grill-with-docs, domain-modeling, codebase-design,
                                    improve-codebase-architecture                               MIT
  anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins architecture, system-design                                 Apache-2.0
  likec4/likec4                     likec4-dsl                                                  MIT
  vercel-labs/agent-skills          react-best-practices, composition-patterns                  MIT (per SKILL.md)
  angular/skills                    angular-developer, angular-new-app                          MIT (per SKILL.md, Google LLC)
  github/awesome-copilot            java-springboot, spring-boot-testing, java-junit            MIT

It also installs, through their official marketplaces and package managers, plugins and tools listed in
config/claude/plugins.json, config/codex/plugins.json, Brewfile and config/npm-globals.txt, each under its own
licence and terms.

Third-party skills installed by devkit are fetched from their upstream repositories at pinned commits and keep their own licences (config/skills.json). In particular:
